exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile mission-vision 1`] = `
"Mission & VisionMissioniWho do you serve first?i 2 maxLondon HomemakersDesigners & Boutique HotelsWhat do you offer them?i 3 maxHomeware CollectionWeaving WorkshopsWhat do they gain?i 2 maxExpressionDevelopmentTo bring slow, handmade craft back into everyday homes: making beautiful, durable textiles from responsibly sourced materials, paying fair prices along our supply chain, and teaching people the skills to make and repair for themselves.VisioniWhere will your customers be?iIn my city / townIn my state / regionAcross my countryIn several countriesWorldwideToday: Across my countryiWhat will your business be when your Vision comes true?i 3 maxServing a large, growing customer baseLoved & recommended by its customersOffering a strong, growing rangeProfitable & paying its own wayKnown & trusted in its fieldRunning smoothly with a strong teamWorking closely with strong partnersBy 2030, to be London's best-known independent weaving studio: a self-sustaining team of eight makers, a collection stocked by twenty UK independent retailers, a waiting list for our workshops, and a verified low-carbon supply chain from sheep to sofa.Back‹›Back
[fields] To bring slow, handmade craft back into everyday homes: making beautiful, durable textiles from responsibly sourced materials, paying fair prices along our supply chain, and teaching people the skills to make and repair for themselves. | By 2030, to be London's best-known independent weaving studio: a self-sustaining team of eight makers, a collection stocked by twenty UK independent retailers, a waiting list for our workshops, and a verified low-carbon supply chain from sheep to sofa."
`;

exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile organization 1`] = `
"OrganisationOrganisationi1.OrganisationOrganisation NameCountryUnited KingdomSelect a country, for example United States of AmericaAustraliaCanadaIrelandNew ZealandUnited KingdomUnited States of AmericaOtherAddressUnit 4, Hackney Wick Maker Yard, 92 Wallis Road London E9 5LNLegal FormiPrivate Company Limited by Shares (Ltd)Select a legal formSole TraderPartnershipLimited Liability Partnership (LLP)Private Company Limited by Shares (Ltd)Private Company Limited by GuaranteeCommunity Interest Company (CIC)Registration DateiOpening DateiActivitiesiPrimarySIC 13921NotesiLumen & Loom Studio Ltd is a London-based textile design studio, founded in 2025 by Maya Chen, Oliver Grant and Priya Shah and based at a shared workshop in Hackney Wick, East London. We design and handweave sustainable home textiles (cushions, throws, table linen and wall hangings) from British wool, organic cotton and recycled yarns. Alongside our own collection we run small-group weaving workshops and take bespoke commissions for interior designers and boutique hotels.Back‹›Back
[fields] Lumen & Loom Studio Ltd | Unit 4, Hackney Wick Maker Yard, 92 Wallis Road
London
E9 5LN | 03/02/2025 | 04/01/2025 | Lumen & Loom Studio Ltd is a London-based textile design studio, founded in 2025 by Maya Chen, Oliver Grant and Priya Shah and based at a shared workshop in Hackney Wick, East London. We design and handweave sustainable home textiles (cushions, throws, table linen and wall hangings) from British wool, organic cotton and recycled yarns. Alongside our own collection we run small-group weaving workshops and take bespoke commissions for interior designers and boutique hotels."
`;

exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile philosophy-manifesto 1`] = `
"Philosophy & ManifestoPhilosophyiWe believe the things we live with shape how we live. A well-made textile, repaired and kept for decades, teaches us to care for what we own. Our work is a small, practical argument for slowness: fewer, better things, made close to home by people you can meet.ManifestoiWe stand for things made slowly and kept for a lifetime. We stand for knowing who made your cushion and where the wool came from. We stand against throwaway homeware, hidden supply chains and craft reduced to a style. Come and see how it's made. Better still, come and make it with us.Back‹›Back
[fields] We believe the things we live with shape how we live. A well-made textile, repaired and kept for decades, teaches us to care for what we own. Our work is a small, practical argument for slowness: fewer, better things, made close to home by people you can meet. | We stand for things made slowly and kept for a lifetime. We stand for knowing who made your cushion and where the wool came from. We stand against throwaway homeware, hidden supply chains and craft reduced to a style. Come and see how it's made. Better still, come and make it with us."
`;

exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile positioning 1`] = `
"Core Market PositioningCore Market PositioningiSeller & Buyer Relationshipi 2 maxB2C (Business-to-Consumer)B2B (Business-to-Business)Buyer's Life-Stagei 2 maxStudents / Young AdultsWorkers / ProfessionalsSeniorsBuyer's category (B2C)iDirect BuyersProxy BuyersDual-Intent BuyersAudience Specialisation & Scalei 2 maxSolopreneurs & FreelancersStartups & SMBsMid-MarketEnterprise or Public SectorBuyer's category (B2B)iDirect BuyersProxy BuyersDual-Intent BuyersPurposei 2 maxLearning & DevelopmentEntertainment & EnjoymentProductivity & EfficiencyBusiness Growth & PerformanceEveryday Needs & ConvenienceHealth, Care & WellbeingGifting & AppreciationSocial Connection & RelationshipsCreation & ExpressionProtection & Risk ReductionCompliance & ObligationsNotesiFor design-conscious Londoners and interior professionals who want homeware with a story, Lumen & Loom is an independent textile studio that makes every piece by hand in London from traceable, low-impact yarns. Each piece is made in a small batch, can be repaired for life, and comes with the name of the weaver who made it, and our studio is open: customers can learn to weave with us. Back‹›Back
[fields] For design-conscious Londoners and interior professionals who want homeware with a story, Lumen & Loom is an independent textile studio that makes every piece by hand in London from traceable, low-impact yarns. Each piece is made in a small batch, can be repaired for life, and comes with the name of the weaver who made it, and our studio is open: customers can learn to weave with us. "
`;

exports[`Lumen & Loom Studio > Identity System › 1. Definition > tile values-principles 1`] = `
"Values & PrinciplesValuesiWhat matters most in how you work?i 2 maxCaring for people & working togetherMaking new & better thingsWinning customers & resultsDoing things right, every time1.Craft over speed2.Honesty about materials and prices3.Care for people and planet4.Openness: share skills, not secrets5.Community before scalePrinciplesi1.Every yarn we use is traceable to its farm or mill.2.We pay everyone we employ or hire to make for us at least the London Living Wage, and the founders reach it as soon as the studio breaks even.3.We repair anything we have made, for life.4.We never discount to clear stock; we make to order instead.5.We decide by consensus of the three founders on anything that affects people or materials.Back‹›Back
[fields] Craft over speed | Honesty about materials and prices | Care for people and planet | Openness: share skills, not secrets | Community before scale | Every yarn we use is traceable to its farm or mill. | We pay everyone we employ or hire to make for us at least the London Living Wage, and the founders reach it as soon as the studio breaks even. | We repair anything we have made, for life. | We never discount to clear stock; we make to order instead. | We decide by consensus of the three founders on anything that affects people or materials."
`;

